# 30_splitfield_lucid.ledc — Split-Field Lucid (~15 min) — different frequency per eye
# Technique: playbook B5 "independent split-field / per-eye". The two eyes are driven at
#            DIFFERENT flicker rates via different channel masks: LEFT eye 16 Hz (a beta
#            'alertness-within-the-dream' cue) and RIGHT eye 6 Hz (theta / dream). Via the
#            optic-chiasm crossover this biases the two hemispheres differently. After a
#            10 Hz alpha induction on BOTH eyes, the field splits, holds, then soft-offs to
#            dark (lucid sessions never wake you).
# Bands: induction alpha 10 Hz (both) -> split LEFT 16 Hz / RIGHT 6 Hz -> soft off.
#
# channel_map recipe (menuconfig CONFIG_LED_CHANNEL_MAP): channels are fixed by temperature/eye
#   (ch0=L-cool bit1, ch1=L-warm bit2, ch2=R-cool bit4, ch3=R-warm bit8). The LEFT eye = mask 3
#   (both L temps, ch0+ch1), the RIGHT eye = mask 12 (both R temps, ch2+ch3), and both eyes = mask
#   15. Map LEFT-eye pixels to channels 0/1 and RIGHT-eye pixels to channels 2/3. For glasses with
#   one pixel per eye: "0,2". For 4 pixels per eye on an 8-pixel strip: "0,1,0,1,2,3,2,3".
#   The masked LED lines then drive each eye independently.
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of
#   photic migraine. Do not use while driving. Experiential, not medical.
#   NOTE: the LEFT eye's 16 Hz sits in the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band, so it is kept
#   DIM (<=18%) and single-eye (never full-field bright) — the validator will WARN on these
#   rows; the dim, half-field delivery is intentional and within the guidelines' brightness
#   cap. If in any doubt, reduce brightness further or avoid. Light ramps in 15 s / out over
#   the final 3 min; cool white (no saturated-red strobe). A lucid session — ends dark.
#
# LED columns: time freq duty bright R G B mask   (mask 3 = left eye, 12 = right, 15 = both)
# Audio: A time freq pan vol mod [ch]   (isochronic 6 Hz theta dream bed)
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the > prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Induction (00:00-02:00): BOTH eyes 10 Hz alpha, dim, fade in ---
0 10 50 >0 180 200 255 15           # both eyes (mask 15) 10 Hz, brightness fade-in from 0
A 0 200 0 >0 6 1                   # isochronic 6 Hz theta dream bed; vol fade-in
S 3000 default 47 "Eyes closed, body still. Let a calm alpha rhythm settle you."
15000 10 50 18 180 200 255 15       # brightness reaches 18% (dim; >=10 s ramp-in)
A 60000 200 0 90 6 1               # audio bed settled 45

# --- Split field (02:00-12:00): LEFT 16 Hz / RIGHT 6 Hz ---
120000 16 50 18 180 200 255 3      # LEFT eye (mask 3): 16 Hz alertness cue — DIM (danger-band; lint warn expected)
120000 6 50 18 180 200 255 12       # RIGHT eye (mask 12): 6 Hz theta / dream
S 120000 default 47 "One eye quickens, one eye slows. Stay aware as you drift into the dream."
S 420000 default 47 "If you notice you are dreaming, stay calm and steady. You are lucid."

# --- Soft Off (12:00-15:00): both eyes + audio fade to dark (no wake-up) ---
720000 16 50 >18 180 200 255 3     # LEFT brightness ramp-out START 18 ...
720000 6 50 >18 180 200 255 12      # RIGHT brightness ramp-out START 18 ...
A 720000 200 0 >90 6 1             # audio bed fade START 45 ...
S 720000 default 47 "Letting the light fade now. Rest, or dream on."
900000 16 50 0 180 200 255 3       # LEFT -> 0
900000 6 50 0 180 200 255 12        # RIGHT -> 0
A 900000 200 0 0 6 1               # audio -> 0
